A category displayed over a total category gives rise to a sigma type.
If C^{\mathtt {D}} : \mathsf {Category}^{\mathtt {D}}\, C and
D^{\mathtt {D}} : \mathsf {Category}^{\mathtt {D}}\, {\mathopen {}\left (\int  C^{\mathtt {D}}\right )\mathclose {}},
then the displayed total category \int ^{\mathtt {D}}D^{\mathtt {D}}
realises the formation rule

\frac {C, x : C^{\mathtt {D}} \vdash  D^{\mathtt {D}}\ \mathsf {Type}}
     {C \vdash  \mathchoice {\textstyle \sum _{{\mathopen {}\left (x : C^{\mathtt {D}}\right )\mathclose {}}}}{\textstyle \sum _{{\mathopen {}\left (x : C^{\mathtt {D}}\right )\mathclose {}}}}{\scriptstyle \sum _{{\mathopen {}\left (x : C^{\mathtt {D}}\right )\mathclose {}}}}{\scriptscriptstyle \sum _{{\mathopen {}\left (x : C^{\mathtt {D}}\right )\mathclose {}}}}{D^{\mathtt {D}}}\ \mathsf {Type}}
